From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:16:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Cover the vendored augmentation module's geometry

Patch 0010 replaced albumentations with a vendored augmentation module and
shipped no tests of its own. The three upstream test modules that touch it live
only in the git tree, and their coverage of it is thin: disabling
`Resize.apply_to_keypoints`, `Resize.apply_to_bboxes` or `Normalize.apply`
entirely leaves all 29 of them green. The geometry -- the arithmetic that
decides where a keypoint or a box lands in a training batch -- was untested,
and an error there does not raise, it silently degrades every model trained
afterwards.

`tests/test_augmentation_geometry.py` pins that arithmetic against
albumentations 1.4.1, the version the port was written against, driven through
`Compose` the way `data/utils.py::apply_transform` drives it: image, keypoints,
bounding boxes and label fields together. Every expected value was measured on
that reference rather than recomputed from the formulas under test.

Covered: `resize` in both `keep_ratio` settings, `longest_max_size`, `hflip`
with and without symmetries, `auto_padding` in every position and both border
modes and both the minimum-size and divisor forms, `affine` rotation about
`((w - 1) / 2, (h - 1) / 2)` and its sign, scaling, pixel translation and the
enclosing box of the rotated corners, the `crop_sampling` origin formula and
its NaN masking for all four sampling methods, `covering`'s half-open holes,
`elastic_transform`'s keypoint displacement, `normalize_images`,
`scale_to_unit_range`, `hist_eq`, `grayscale`, the `label_fields` bookkeeping
that keeps surviving boxes aligned with their labels, and the empty-keypoint,
empty-box and both-empty cases.

Thirty-four source mutations were used to check the tests can fail -- among
them returning keypoints unscaled from `Resize`, mirroring keypoints about
`width` instead of `width - 1`, transposing the padding offsets, rotating about
`(w / 2, h / 2)`, negating the rotation angle, dropping the `+ 1` from the crop
origin, closing the far edge of a dropout hole, skipping the mean subtraction in
`Normalize`, and keeping the labels of dropped boxes. All thirty-four are
killed.

Seven behaviours that albumentations 1.4.1 had and the vendored module does not
are recorded as strict xfails, so repairing one turns into an XPASS and forces
the marker to be removed rather than letting the deviation survive another
review:

* a crop larger than the image returns a wrong-sized array instead of raising;
* `Compose(seed=...)` re-seeds on every call, collapsing an epoch of
  augmentations to a single one;
* an `affine` config block missing `rotation`, `scaling` or `translation`
  raises `TypeError` instead of defaulting that parameter to the identity;
* `MotionBlur` draws its kernel size from {3,4,5,6,7} and rounds even values up,
  so P(3) is 0.20 rather than the reference's 1/3, and the mean kernel grows
  from 4.99 to 5.40;
* `GaussNoise` draws sigma uniformly rather than as the root of a uniform
  variance, so under the shipped `gaussian_noise: 12.75` the mean sigma falls
  from 8.5 to 6.375 -- the same support, about 24% less noise.
